{"name":"Cotton Knit","hex":"#e5dfd2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cotton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fibrous substance:\n A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium.\n Any similar soft, fibrous, white substance of fine hairs, of any origin.","A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of cotton."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotton"},{"term":"knit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn thread or yarn into a piece of fabric by forming loops that are pulled through each other. This can be done by hand with needles or by machine.","To create a stitch by pulling the working yarn through an existing stitch from back to front."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A knitted garment.","A session of knitting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cotton","blocks":[{"text":"Cotton is a soft, fluffy staple fiber that grows in a boll, or protective case, around the seeds of the cotton plants of the genus Gossypium in the mallow family Malvaceae. The fiber is almost pure cellulose and may contain minor percentages of waxes, fats, pectins, and water. Under natural conditions, cotton bolls facilitate the dispersal of the seeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CottonPlant.JPG/330px-CottonPlant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton"},{"title":"Knitting","blocks":[{"text":"Knitting is the process of interlooping yarn to create textile fabric made of interconnected loops, done by hand, machine or both."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Oma_strickt_Str%C3%BCmpfe.jpg/330px-Oma_stric